  note right of Q_E02
    Reached only from Q_E01 = Yes.
    The BR "field hidden if Q1 is set at No" is expressed
    as routing, not as a visibility rule - an unreached
    question is blank, which is the same outcome.
  end note

  note right of Q_E03
    **Computed. Value rules, first match wins:**

    field goCeFedLeverageRatio range [>0]
      AND field goCeFedLeverageRatio < 1 x field goCeEscalationThreshold -> NO
    Q_E01 is NO   -> YES
    Q_E02 is YES  -> YES
    Q_E01 is YES  -> NO

    NOTE: a range bound must be a NUMERIC LITERAL (BOUND pattern in
    ConditionExpressionParser), so a field key cannot appear inside
    range [..]. The threshold test is a separate AND atom using the
    "n x field" form with a multiplier of 1.

    **There is deliberately no "*" catch-all.**
    An NA (undefined) ratio matches no rule and the question
    keeps no value - this is the "= empty" outcome.
    The last line is the BR's "Else No": it is reachable only
    when Q_E01 was actually asked, which means the ratio was defined.

    **OPEN - Clara:** the written cascade in Section 1.1 falls through
    to "Else No" for an NA ratio; the flowchart says "empty".
    Empty means the test did not apply, No means it applied and passed.
    Authored here per the flowchart.

    **OPEN - Clara:** in the flowchart the True/False labels on the
    "Threshold for Escalation < 0" diamond are transposed - as drawn,
    both branches of the ">= 6x" diamond reach the same box.
    Authored here per the Section 1.1 text (<6x and >0 -> No).
  end note

