  note as MANDATORY_RULE
    **Mandatory questions**
    Every question presented after Main Industry is mandatory, EXCEPT:
      - APLC_PATH_Q08 (Comment)              - not mandatory
      - REIT_PATH_COMMENT_TEXTAREA (Comment) - not mandatory
      - PROJECT_FINANCE_PATH_Q07             - IS mandatory
      - COMPUTED questions (PROJECT_FINANCE_Q04, Q_E03, APLC_PATH_Q07,
        REIT_PATH_Q03_A) and DERIVED questions (Q_S05, BNPP_COUNTERPARTY_RATING,
        SP_ISSUER_RATING, MOODYS_ISSUER_RATING) - the analyst cannot answer
        these, so a MANDATORY rule would deadlock the form.

    One Forms-tab row PER QUESTION, each with its own static message:
      "FED Form - The question "<label>" is mandatory"
    Violations accumulate and clear individually, so no runtime interpolation
    is needed - every message is a literal string, as in ECB.

    **Percent scale** (confirmed with Clara): stored at 28 decimal places as a
    fraction (0.60, 0.08, 0.85); the UI renders 60% / 8% / 85%. Both sides of
    every threshold comparison are therefore on the same scale.
  end note


  note as GRAMMAR_NOTES
    **Checked against ConditionExpressionParser / ConditionEvaluator**

    1. OR does not exist - only AND. It is not needed: value rules and branches
       are FIRST MATCH WINS, so a top-level OR becomes one line per alternative
       with the same target, and an OR nested under a gate distributes into
       gate AND alternative lines. Worked example, APLC, 7 lines, no OR:

         Q-HSD100 is YES                                                     -> FED_NOT_LEVERAGED
         Q01 is YES                                                          -> FED_LEVERAGED_HIGH_RISK
         field aplcDebtToEquityRatio >= 1 x field aplcDebtToEquityLeverageThreshold AND Q-WLDD is YES -> FED_LEVERAGED_HIGH_RISK
         field aplcDebtToEquityRatio range [<0] AND Q-WLDD is YES            -> FED_LEVERAGED_HIGH_RISK
         field aplcDebtToEquityRatio >= 1 x field aplcDebtToEquityLeverageThreshold -> FED_LEVERAGED_LOW_RISK
         field aplcDebtToEquityRatio range [<0]                              -> FED_LEVERAGED_LOW_RISK
         *                                                                   -> FED_NOT_LEVERAGED

    2. Own answer AND another question IS supported. A bare token parses to a
       condition with no questionKey, and the evaluator resolves that against
       the OWNING question; AND-composites evaluate every child against the same
       owner. So the shared-question collapse is safe:

         YES AND Q-MI01 is REIT -> <ratings block>
         *                      -> <subsidiary-of-IG question>

    3. Field-to-field comparison exists only as "field A <op> n x field B".
       Use a multiplier of 1 to compare a ratio against a threshold FIELD rather
       than hardcoding the number in the condition.

    4. An absent or non-numeric value matches NOTHING - every path in
       ConditionEvaluator returns false. So an uncomputable ratio falls through
       to "*". The blocking errors on the zero-denominator fields are what keeps
       that from silently producing FED_NOT_LEVERAGED on a saved analysis.

    **OPEN - engine change needed**: reitAdjustedTotalCommittedDebt has a
    BRANCHING formula (carve-out yes/no). Field formulas are single expressions;
    only question value rules branch, and a value rule assigns a literal, not an
    arithmetic result - so this cannot be modelled as value rules today.
    PROPOSAL: give fields an ordered "Formula Rules" cell reusing the same
    first-match-wins shape and the same ConditionExpressionParser:
        field reitCarveOutHighlySecuredDebt is NO -> reitTotalCommittedDebtPerDefinition
        *                                         -> reitTotalCommittedDebtPerDefinition - reitHighlySecuredPortionCommittedTotalDebt
  end note


